  "title": "A Dead Star Is Ringed by Two Gas Rings. What Made Them? #shorts",
  "description": "Astronomers report that the white dwarf WD J1328-1450, about 1,600 light years away, is surrounded by two separate rings of gas rather than one disc. A study in Nature Astronomy proposes two surviving rocky bodies sculpt the rings; they have not been detected, and an unresolved double white dwarf is an alternative.\n\nSources: Nature Astronomy paper (Gentile Fusillo et al.), ESO release eso2613, Phys.org, Universe Today, Nautilus.\n\n#science #astronomy #whitedwarf #ESO",
